text:
@asianstud7 I agree SpaceX is more well positioned to eat into the big 3's lunch than Dish since they actually have a working internet network in Starlink.  Dish never had the funds to get the network up and running and burned through all their cash acquiring spectrum licenses without a well thought out plan to deploy the spectrum. 

Also the fact that the frequencies SpaceX acquired from Dish and Grain already have 5G band support by the 3GPP helps with getting the handset makers to add support to them easily.  

The biggest challenge assuming the FCC will approve the sale (I can't see why not) is getting the terrestrial network up and running to deploy the 800 MHz and 2 GHz spectrum.
